# Audited: one tick clicks tap (an answer to both row buttons, due next tick) and drops row 2 through the forwarded text input; row 2's label leaves in that tick's patch, and in the owed tick only row 1 hears the tap.
# The teardown's tests: declarations of sem-ch09-host-teardown.prism (Semantics chapter 9).

test a_left_key_drops_the_answer_in_flight, @host:
    build
        => expect Ui.Label(text="two: 0")
    click at 0, send at 1/[0]/0, Backspace
        => expect_none Ui.Label(text="two: 0")
        => expect Ui.Label(text="one: 0")
    compute
        => expect Ui.Label(text="one: 1")
        => expect_count Ui.Label(..), 1
